id: pm-rust-native-changes
title: Resume native agents from bounded incremental mutation cursors
description: Pull-based native transport for canonical mutation events; read-only local history adapter and versioned adapter capability.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: cursor,events,native
created_at: "2026-10-27T16:36:18.810Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T19:45:25.327Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Concurrent appends resume after the last admitted event exactly once; Stale cursors and unsupported adapters return typed refusals with remedies; Cancellation and backpressure remain bounded without Node or Git; Typed SDK, compact TOON and JSON CLI, documentation, seeded property and interleaving tests, public tracker validation, npm and Bun CI gates"
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T16:36:27.058Z",codex-agent,"Overlap checked against the pinned public SDK mutation-events declarations, native_adapter and read_session, and pm-context since.ts. Core listMutationEvents and subscribeMutationEventBatches own the compact event projection; pm-context owns delta ranking. This work adds native pull transport using that projection, with per-stream immutable prefix cursors so backdated concurrent appends remain visible. No import/export/sync, item writes, status interpretation, ranking, shared checkpoints or new event schema. Reuse existing native adapter admission and canonical history hashing/codecs; preserve backend refusals. Registry current CLI is 2026.10.27; retain the pinned 2026.10.21 oracle."
  "2026-10-27T16:43:14.500Z",codex-agent,"Implemented ChangeReader and LocalChangeAdapter, additive changes ABI capability and one-page changes CLI. Native prefix cursors are caller-owned and immutable; independent readers do not share checkpoint state. The local path performs no item mutation, import/export/sync, status decision, lease or retry. Targeted SDK tests pass 7/7, including a fixed-seed 500-sequence model with older-input replay, CRLF and relationship-patch preservation read back through Workspace.history. No normalization oracle is duplicated. Continuing strict output fuzzing, step-boundary interleavings, revert proof, read-only public-data validation and CI coverage."
  "2026-10-27T17:16:11.723Z",codex-agent,"Final overlap refresh: current CLI 2026.10.27 history events exposes resumable NDJSON, verify and provenance; pm-web resume-packets/history-read-gate consume core listMutationEvents; pm-context since owns ranked deltas. The native surface deliberately reuses the compact event fields and existing ABI, with no new ranking, write/sync path or backend. The local adapter uses physical stream prefixes rather than timestamp ordering so late appends cannot disappear. Scope: integer-only admission decisions; no status-role or relationship interpretation and no ambient create/update defaults. Public-copy validation: 86 items, 178 source files, 4519252 bytes, 2266 canonical events, 114 pages, 17141 max page bytes, 13994 max cursor bytes, 0 idle events, SDK equality and unchanged read-only copy; no Node/Git on native path. Final module coverage: 364 lines, 33 functions, 549 regions and 82 branches, all 100 percent. Four behavioral reverts fail in a disposable copy; fixed tests pass again. First pm-linked run hit its default 120-second compile timeout under shared-host load; retrying serially with a 900-second bound. Full npm/Bun gate evidence will come from CI."
  "2026-10-27T17:25:34.814Z",codex-agent,"PR ready for review: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/126 . All three linked commands passed with the bounded serial retry: SDK 12/12, no-Git/no-Node CLI 1/1, writer failure propagation 1/1; zero assertion failures or timeouts in the retry. The earlier default timeout is superseded by those receipts. Rustfmt, all-target clippy, Rust documentation, TypeScript typecheck/lint, changelog generation/check, 4 behavioral revert proofs, full new-module coverage and public-copy validation pass. Initial CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/40550045531 is queued on the implementation commit; this final tracker handoff will trigger fresh exact-head npm/Bun release gates. Gate counts and final run URL belong to the PR acceptance table after that verification. The item remains in progress for orchestrator verification and closure; releasing only this author claim. No new pm CLI or SDK defect was found."
  "2026-10-27T17:37:05.719Z",codex-agent,"Final self-review found a transport-correlation gap in the new SDK: a constant request ID cannot distinguish a delayed older page after multiple successful pulls. Binding correlation to the full cursor-bearing request and adding a genuine local-adapter delayed-reply regression. This stays within the exactly-once/stale-adapter acceptance criteria; no upstream SDK defect is involved. Reclaimed only this item for the correction; a fresh exact-head CI run will follow."
  "2026-10-27T17:46:17.911Z",codex-agent,"Added a genuine local-adapter test that succeeds twice, injects the first reply on the third exchange, verifies typed correlation refusal without cursor movement, then receives version three exactly once. Correlation now hashes the existing native per-call nonce together with the full cursor/control request, avoiding clock-based event positions and metadata leakage. The page boundary also refuses duplicate physical identities across events and skip receipts. New focused regressions pass; refreshing the six-case revert proof, linked tests, coverage and public-copy validation before the next head."
  "2026-10-27T18:28:44.875Z",codex-agent,"Correlation/dedup correction complete. All linked commands pass: SDK 14/14, CLI 1/1, writer failures 1/1, with zero failures/ignored tests. Six behavioral reverts fail as required; the managed subprocess runner also passes its selected proof. Refreshed focused coverage is 100 percent: 384 lines, 37 functions, 574 regions, 84 branches. Clippy, private/public Rust docs, fmt, TypeScript typecheck/lint pass. The corrected debug artifact repeats public validation: 86 items, 178 files, 4519252 source bytes, 2266 canonical events, 114 pages, 17141 maximum page bytes, 13994 maximum cursor bytes; unchanged read-only copy and no Node/Git on the native path. Validation report records the new artifact/copy digests and 126281 ms measured wall time. Prior CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/40550856854 remains queued on the parent head; the corrected head will get fresh full npm/Bun aggregates, with exact URL/counts in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/126 . Latest branch CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/workflows/ci.yml?query=branch%3Afeat%2Fnative-incremental-change-readers . No full gate is claimed from queued or skipped jobs. Final tracker writes now complete; releasing this author claim and leaving closure to the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-27T18:43:22.165Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40560731873: macOS npm aggregate reached the tests and reported 349 pass, 1 failure. The new source-file-kind fixture attempted to create a non-UTF-8 filename; macOS rejected it with Illegal byte sequence before reader admission. The 500-sequence and cursor/correlation tests passed. Replacing that filesystem assumption with a pure path-byte refusal test, keeping the Linux real-file case and adding a real-tracker filename-admission fault boundary for every platform. This is a package fixture defect, not an SDK gap. Reclaimed for the correction; fresh exact-head CI will follow."
  "2026-10-27T19:03:20.522Z",codex-agent,"Portable filename correction verified: byte-path tests run independently of filesystem filename policy; Linux still exercises an actual invalid-name file, and real-tracker I/O boundary injection covers filename-admission failure on every platform. Linked commands now pass SDK 15/15, CLI 1/1 and writer 1/1, zero failures/ignored. Seven behavioral reverts fail as required. New module coverage remains 100 percent: 392 lines, 39 functions, 588 regions, 84 branches. Clippy, Rust docs, fmt, TypeScript typecheck/lint pass. Public-copy validation refreshed for the corrected binary: 86 items, 178 source files, 4519252 bytes, 2266 SDK-matching events over 114 pages; max page 17141 bytes, max cursor 13994, zero idle events, unchanged source and no Node/Git. Report records exact artifact and copy digests. Parent run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/40560731873 passed Ubuntu/Windows full Rust and latency probes but failed the superseded macOS fixture; it is not final acceptance. Fresh npm/Bun aggregate evidence will be taken only from the next exact head and linked in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/126 . Final tracker writes complete; releasing the claim and retaining in_progress for orchestrator closure."
  "2026-10-27T19:38:58.762Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head macOS release tests pass, but the aggregate coverage gate reports two uncovered CLI regions while the new reader module remains at 100 percent. Keeping all four repository floors at 100 percent; adding direct CLI success and refusal coverage before a fresh exact-head CI run."
  "2026-10-27T19:39:08.507Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head macOS release tests pass, but the aggregate coverage gate reports two uncovered CLI regions while the new reader module remains at 100 percent. Keeping all four repository floors at 100 percent; adding direct CLI success and refusal coverage before a fresh exact-head CI run."
  "2026-10-27T19:45:17.012Z",codex-agent,"Coverage correction: all 39 CLI unit tests pass, and targeted nightly coverage shows no uncovered regions in the changes dispatch, including the two spans missed by the macOS aggregate. The pinned pm runner also passes the updated CLI test (1/1). This correction changes tests and validation notes only; the validated binary digest and public-data measurements remain unchanged. New reader SDK tests remain 15/15 and the non-git CLI contract remains 1/1. Seven disposable behavioral revert proofs are retained. Fresh final-head npm and Bun release gates remain required; follow the branch CI workflow and PR 126 for exact run URLs and pending/completed counts. No item is closed; verification belongs to the orchestrator. CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/workflows/ci.yml?query=branch%3Afeat%2Fnative-incremental-change-readers PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/126"
